===== README_FIRST.md =====
     1  # Read this first
     2  
     3  This is a frozen, self-contained referee handoff for *A fitness-independent
     4  family of simultaneous amplifiers beyond relative fitness 3/2*.  It is meant
     5  for an independent, submission-style audit of the manuscript and its exact
     6  certificate programs.  It does not prescribe a favorable verdict.
     7  
     8  Start by reading `REFEREE_PROMPT.md`.  Inspect the manuscript, replay entry
     9  point, and every invoked program before running the convenience command.
    10  `CLAIM_CODE_MAP.md` is only a navigation index, and
    11  `REFEREE_REPORT_TEMPLATE.md` is optional.
    12  
    13  ## Frozen identity
    14  
    15  - Scientific source commit: `2302d7c6ae17fc061a985da322df6d0600b66672`
    16  - Immutable source tag: `simultaneous-amplification-beyond-three-halves-v2.0.1`
    17  - Source archive SHA-256: `ce62bfbdb22681ba48b2a04653155b2e06f52659f140c13f5e0220db365b9250`
    18  - Manuscript PDF SHA-256: `f68142b3d99b95f83ca6ba4688539cb9e0fdb88ed96809aef5316ed22a59888f`
    19  - Source archive: `simultaneous_amplifier_beyond_three_halves_source_and_certificates.tar.gz`
    20  - Detached archive checksum: `simultaneous_amplifier_beyond_three_halves_source_and_certificates.tar.gz.sha256`
    21  - Whole-package manifest: `PACKAGE_MANIFEST.sha256`
    22  - Internal source-archive members: 19
    23  
    24  The wrapper package may be added by a later commit.  The scientific source
    25  commit and tag above identify the state from which the source archive and PDF
    26  were generated, avoiding a self-referential package hash.
    27  
    28  ## Layout
    29  
    30  - `simultaneous_amplification_beyond_three_halves.pdf`: convenience copy of
    31    the compiled manuscript.
    32  - `simultaneous_amplifier_beyond_three_halves_source_and_certificates.tar.gz`:
    33    deterministic source, certificate, and replay archive supplied with the
    34    manuscript.
    35  - `source_and_certificates/`: byte-identical extraction of that archive for
    36    immediate inspection.
    37  - `verify_referee_package.py`: standard-library integrity verifier.
    38  - `run_all_referee_checks.sh`: package verification, pinned replay,
    39    deterministic source-archive and PDF rebuilds, and byte comparisons in a
    40    disposable directory.
    41  
    42  Prior referee verdicts, hostile-audit ledgers, submission correspondence, and
    43  saved successful output are deliberately absent.  The source archive does
    44  include provenance and research logs; treat every statement in those files as
    45  an author claim, not evidence.
    46  
    47  ## Suggested order
    48  
    49  1. Read the PDF and LaTeX source and make an independent theorem ledger.
    50  2. Inspect the wrapper runner and integrity checker, `bootstrap_replay.sh`,
    51     `replay.sh`, `build.sh`, `requirements.txt`, every verifier invoked, and
    52     all imported code.
    53  3. Verify package identity with
    54     `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 verify_referee_package.py`.
    55  4. With Python 3.14.6 available, run `./run_all_referee_checks.sh`.  If
    56     `python3` is not that interpreter, set
    57     `BOOTSTRAP_PYTHON=/path/to/python3.14.6`.
    58  5. Complete the mathematical and software audit described in the neutral
    59     prompt and record any limitation that prevents a complete check.
    60  
    61  The replay pins SymPy 1.14.0 and mpmath 1.3.0.  The PDF rebuild requires
    62  Tectonic 0.16.9 and Poppler 26.08.0 (`pdfinfo` and `pdftoppm`).  The bootstrap
    63  may access the configured Python package index to install pinned dependencies;
    64  those dependencies are version-pinned but their distribution files are not
    65  vendored or hash-pinned.  A document rebuild may also populate Tectonic's
    66  standard resource-bundle cache.  Run untrusted review material in an
    67  unprivileged disposable environment without personal credentials.
===== VERSION.md =====
     1  # Frozen version record
     2  
     3  - Manuscript: *A fitness-independent family of simultaneous amplifiers beyond
     4    relative fitness 3/2*
     5  - Author: Alec Kriebel
     6  - ORCID: 0009-0001-9320-500X
     7  - Package date: 2026-08-22 (America/Los_Angeles)
