 1467 \section*{Statements and Declarations}
 1468 
 1469 \noindent\textbf{Data and code availability.}
 1470 No empirical data are used.  The LaTeX source, exact symbolic and rational
 1471 verifiers, labelled-chain audit, and pinned build and replay scripts accompany
 1472 this revision as the deterministic Supplementary Material archive
 1473 \nolinkurl{simultaneous_amplifier_beyond_three_halves_source_and_certificates.tar.gz}.
 1474 It contains an internal SHA-256 manifest and a fresh-environment bootstrap.
 1475 The corresponding development sources are in the
 1476 \href{https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/tree/simultaneous-amplification-beyond-three-halves-v2.0.1/universal_simultaneous_amplification/phase4_landmark_closure/paper_hybrid_threshold}{paper-specific frozen repository directory}.
 1477 The full-repository software snapshot at
 1478 \href{https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21852072}{doi:10.5281/zenodo.21852072}
 1479 contains the unrefereed v1
 1480 manuscript, source, and software, not this superseding revision.  No new
 1481 persistent identifier has yet been assigned.  When this revision is posted
 1482 as a preprint, the same frozen bundle will be deposited alongside it and this
 1483 statement updated with the assigned identifier.
 1484 The replay enumerates all $512$ configurations and $108$ orbit fibres of its
 1485 finite audit graph and independently checks the response algebra, rational
 1486 margins, Sturm isolation, and tangency.  These certificates audit finite
 1487 transition aggregation and exact algebra; the weak-cut and population
 1488 asymptotics are analytic proofs in the manuscript, not computer-assisted
 1489 consequences of the replay.
 1490 
 1491 \medskip
 1492 \noindent\textbf{Funding.}
 1493 No external funding supported this work.
